# Search exclusions (ripgrep — what Claude Code's Grep and Glob run on).
#
# These trees are vendored or generated: nothing here is ours to change, and a
# fix applied inside one is reverted by the next `make update-skills` /
# `make arsenal-upgrade` / `init.py` refresh. `pyproject.toml` already excludes
# the same paths from ruff and mypy for exactly that reason — this is the third
# tool that should not be reading them.
#
# The cost is not only noise. `vendor/claude-arsenal/docs/research/` holds a
# 2.9MB research document whose lines run to several thousand words each, so a
# single repository-wide grep that happens to match inside it returns thousands
# of tokens of irrelevant prose in one result.
#
# `!` re-includes a path. Search a vendored tree deliberately with
# `rg --no-ignore-vcs -u` or by naming its directory as the search path.

vendor/
claude-arsenal/bin/
claude-arsenal/scripts/
.claude/skills/skill-creator/references/

# Generated readers — the committed HTML/annotated copies of specs that live in
# source form elsewhere. Matching both means every spec hit is reported twice.
docs/spec-v2/spec-reader.html
docs/spec-v2-steps/spec-reader.html

# Caches and build output.
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
